# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# eol=lf (not just text=auto) is the half that matters: it pins the CHECKOUT, so a
# Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true cannot write CRs back in. Without it, a
# Windows write turns an index into CRLF (one CR per line) and a later tool that
# treats a lone CR as a line terminator rewrites it with LF only -- every CR
# becoming a real blank line. LL-G's master index went 257 -> 3071 lines that way
# while its actual content stayed flat, and "update one entry count" landed as a
# 768-insertion diff. Fix the cause here rather than re-collapsing blank runs later.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must use LF line endings, or the shebang breaks on
# Git Bash/macOS/Linux with "bad interpreter: bash\r".
*.sh text eol=lf
